config MCUX_HAS_COMPONENT_driver.dual_adc
    bool
    default y if MCUX_HW_IP_DriverType_DADC

config MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.dual_adc
    bool "dual_adc"
    select MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.common
    depends on MCUX_HAS_COMPONENT_driver.dual_adc

if MCUX_COMPONENT_driver.dual_adc
    config DUALADC_RESET_TIMEOUT
        int "NOP loop count to hold CTRL[RSTA]/CTRL[RSTB] asserted during software reset"
        default 20
        help
            CTRL[RSTA] and CTRL[RSTB] are NOT self-clearing. The logic high level must
            be sustained for more than 2 ADC functional clock cycles before the reset
            takes effect; the bits are then cleared explicitly by software.

            This value controls how many __NOP() iterations DUALADC_Init executes
            between asserting and releasing the reset bits, providing a portable hold
            time that adapts to different CPU and ADC clock frequency combinations.

            The required count scales with the CPU-to-ADC clock frequency ratio:
              min_count = ceil(2 * f_CPU / f_ADC)
            The default of 20 covers ratios up to 10 (e.g., 150 MHz CPU with a
            16 MHz ADC clock). Increase this value when the CPU clock is much faster
            than the ADC functional clock (i.e., when f_CPU/f_ADC is large) to
            ensure the minimum 2 ADC clock cycle hold time is always met.

    config DUALADC_CALIBRATION_TIMEOUT
        int "Max loops to wait for each DualADC calibration step to complete (0 means wait forever)"
        default 0
        help
            Maximum number of loop iterations for each polling step inside DUALADC_DoCalibration:
            offset calibration (STAT0[CAL_RDY]), high-speed calibration (STAT0[CAL_RDY]),
            gain calibration hardware completion (GCC[n][RDY]), and final CAL_RDY confirmation.
            If set to 0, each step waits indefinitely until completion.
endif
